WEBVTT

00:00:00.040 --> 00:00:02.880
In late July, an unusual alliance formed

00:00:02.880 --> 00:00:04.200
in Washington.

00:00:04.240 --> 00:00:07.020
NVIDIA, Microsoft, and other technology

00:00:07.020 --> 00:00:08.870
heavyweights argued that open-weight

00:00:08.870 --> 00:00:10.730
artificial intelligence should remain

00:00:10.740 --> 00:00:11.800
open.

00:00:11.840 --> 00:00:13.760
A striking position from companies that

00:00:13.760 --> 00:00:16.480
also sell the chips, cloud, and software

00:00:16.480 --> 00:00:17.320
around it.

00:00:17.360 --> 00:00:19.480
That sounds like a policy dispute.

00:00:19.520 --> 00:00:22.120
It is also a stock market story, because

00:00:22.200 --> 00:00:24.210
the question is not simply whether open

00:00:24.210 --> 00:00:25.670
models are good or bad.

00:00:25.760 --> 00:00:27.620
The question is more uncomfortable.

00:00:27.660 --> 00:00:30.140
If capable models become widely available,

00:00:30.180 --> 00:00:32.370
which part of the AI economy keeps the

00:00:32.420 --> 00:00:34.920
profit, start in the United States.

00:00:34.960 --> 00:00:37.240
On the 24th of July, the open model

00:00:37.360 --> 00:00:40.000
argument arrived in front of lawmakers.

00:00:40.040 --> 00:00:41.950
The companies were not promising that

00:00:41.950 --> 00:00:43.430
openness is free.

00:00:43.480 --> 00:00:45.760
They were arguing that a wider ecosystem

00:00:45.840 --> 00:00:47.540
can make the United States more

00:00:47.540 --> 00:00:49.840
competitive and keep one gatekeeper from

00:00:49.840 --> 00:00:51.610
owning every route into artificial

00:00:51.610 --> 00:00:52.430
intelligence.

00:00:52.520 --> 00:00:54.040
Now rotate east.

00:00:54.080 --> 00:00:56.150
China is no longer a footnote in this

00:00:56.150 --> 00:00:56.760
story.

00:00:56.800 --> 00:00:59.680
On the 17th of July, Moonshot AI unveiled

00:00:59.680 --> 00:01:02.210
Kimi K3, a model it described as the

00:01:02.210 --> 00:01:04.520
world's largest open-weight system at two,

00:01:04.820 --> 00:01:06.760
eight trillion parameters.

00:01:06.800 --> 00:01:09.080
Days later, Moonshot temporarily paused

00:01:09.200 --> 00:01:11.670
new subscriptions after demand strained

00:01:11.670 --> 00:01:12.600
capacity.

00:01:12.640 --> 00:01:14.890
Alibaba was previewing its own enormous

00:01:14.890 --> 00:01:17.200
model before an open-weight release.

00:01:17.240 --> 00:01:18.660
That sequence tells us something

00:01:18.660 --> 00:01:19.320
important.

00:01:19.360 --> 00:01:20.930
Open access can lower the toll on

00:01:20.980 --> 00:01:23.020
intelligence and still create a queue at

00:01:23.020 --> 00:01:24.520
the infrastructure layer.

00:01:24.560 --> 00:01:26.280
Here is the vocabulary.

00:01:26.320 --> 00:01:28.160
Open-weight does not necessarily mean

00:01:28.160 --> 00:01:29.780
fully open source.

00:01:29.820 --> 00:01:31.520
It usually means the trained parameters

00:01:31.520 --> 00:01:33.650
are released so developers can download a

00:01:33.650 --> 00:01:36.310
model, run it themselves, fine tune it, or

00:01:36.310 --> 00:01:38.490
build a private system around it.

00:01:38.600 --> 00:01:40.890
The training data, the full recipe, the

00:01:41.000 --> 00:01:42.610
safety process, and the expensive

00:01:42.610 --> 00:01:45.200
infrastructure may still remain closed.

00:01:45.260 --> 00:01:46.340
The difference matters.

00:01:46.380 --> 00:01:48.630
A closed model is a service you rent.

00:01:48.680 --> 00:01:50.400
An open-weight model is closer to a

00:01:50.400 --> 00:01:52.720
machine you can take home and modify.

00:01:52.760 --> 00:01:54.720
That can weaken a provider's pricing

00:01:54.720 --> 00:01:55.260
power.

00:01:55.300 --> 00:01:57.340
Customers can negotiate harder.

00:01:57.380 --> 00:01:59.530
Developers can keep sensitive workloads on

00:01:59.530 --> 00:02:00.840
their own machines.

00:02:00.880 --> 00:02:02.690
Startups can build without depending on

00:02:02.690 --> 00:02:04.890
one company's permission, price, or

00:02:05.000 --> 00:02:07.830
product roadmap, but cheaper intelligence

00:02:07.830 --> 00:02:09.320
can create more demand.

00:02:09.360 --> 00:02:11.220
When a useful capability becomes

00:02:11.220 --> 00:02:13.300
inexpensive, people usually find more

00:02:13.300 --> 00:02:15.310
things to do with it, more agents, more

00:02:15.620 --> 00:02:17.940
automation, more experiments, and more

00:02:17.940 --> 00:02:18.690
inference.

00:02:18.800 --> 00:02:20.440
This is where the map rotates from the

00:02:20.440 --> 00:02:22.200
model to the stack beneath it.

00:02:22.240 --> 00:02:24.430
Look at China's Guangdong Province.

00:02:24.500 --> 00:02:27.120
In May, large data center clusters entered

00:02:27.190 --> 00:02:29.600
electricity spot trading as virtual power

00:02:29.600 --> 00:02:32.490
plants, a real world sign that AI demand

00:02:32.540 --> 00:02:34.720
is becoming a grid problem, not just a

00:02:34.720 --> 00:02:36.120
software problem.

00:02:36.160 --> 00:02:37.360
Then look at Taiwan.

00:02:37.400 --> 00:02:39.900
The chip factory is part of the AI story

00:02:39.940 --> 00:02:42.520
before the model ever reaches a customer.

00:02:42.560 --> 00:02:44.350
The chain continues through Japan's

00:02:44.350 --> 00:02:46.720
equipment makers, South Korea's memory

00:02:46.720 --> 00:02:49.080
industry, the Netherlands lithography

00:02:49.080 --> 00:02:52.120
ecosystem, and American cloud campuses.

00:02:52.160 --> 00:02:54.450
The International Energy Agency's base

00:02:54.560 --> 00:02:57.120
case puts global data center electricity

00:02:57.240 --> 00:03:01.920
use at about 945 terawatt hours in 2030.

00:03:01.960 --> 00:03:03.850
That is not a prediction of one company's

00:03:03.850 --> 00:03:04.480
revenue.

00:03:04.520 --> 00:03:06.700
It is a reminder that every extra layer of

00:03:06.700 --> 00:03:09.030
software eventually touches a physical

00:03:09.030 --> 00:03:09.570
system.

00:03:09.720 --> 00:03:11.600
Open models can reduce the price of

00:03:11.600 --> 00:03:13.550
software while increasing the volume of

00:03:13.550 --> 00:03:15.600
hardware, networking, cooling, and

00:03:15.600 --> 00:03:17.690
electricity required to run it.

00:03:17.840 --> 00:03:20.920
Now rotate to New York, Tokyo, and Seoul.

00:03:20.960 --> 00:03:23.150
Markets do not price possibilities.

00:03:23.200 --> 00:03:25.040
They price expectations.

00:03:25.080 --> 00:03:27.810
The IMF says AI exposed markets in the

00:03:27.810 --> 00:03:29.240
United States, Japan.

00:03:29.280 --> 00:03:31.720
South Korea and Taiwan outperformed in the

00:03:31.800 --> 00:03:34.070
second quarter of 2026.

00:03:34.120 --> 00:03:36.480
That is a broad market signal, not proof

00:03:36.480 --> 00:03:39.170
that every AI investment will pay off.

00:03:39.220 --> 00:03:41.500
The BIS warning is the other half of the

00:03:41.500 --> 00:03:42.300
picture.

00:03:42.340 --> 00:03:44.400
When valuations and earnings expectations

00:03:44.400 --> 00:03:47.170
are already high, a disappointment in AI

00:03:47.170 --> 00:03:49.690
revenue, utilization, or capital spending

00:03:50.000 --> 00:03:52.380
can travel quickly through the market.

00:03:52.480 --> 00:03:54.920
If open models make applications cheaper

00:03:54.960 --> 00:03:57.010
and adoption faster, investors may reward

00:03:57.320 --> 00:04:00.040
the companies that own distribution, data,

00:04:00.040 --> 00:04:02.040
and customer relationships.

00:04:02.080 --> 00:04:04.300
If model prices collapse before massive

00:04:04.300 --> 00:04:06.190
infrastructure spending pays back,

00:04:06.260 --> 00:04:08.040
investors may punish the companies

00:04:08.080 --> 00:04:10.560
carrying the heaviest expectations.

00:04:10.600 --> 00:04:12.320
The same technology can be good for

00:04:12.320 --> 00:04:14.910
adoption and bad for a particular business

00:04:14.910 --> 00:04:15.480
model.

00:04:15.520 --> 00:04:16.680
So who wins?

00:04:16.720 --> 00:04:19.010
Chip and memory suppliers may benefit from

00:04:19.120 --> 00:04:21.430
wider deployment, but hardware pricing can

00:04:21.430 --> 00:04:22.360
still compress.

00:04:22.400 --> 00:04:24.890
Cloud companies may sell more compute, but

00:04:24.890 --> 00:04:26.850
they also have to finance the data

00:04:26.850 --> 00:04:27.580
centers.

00:04:27.620 --> 00:04:29.470
Software companies may gain bargaining

00:04:29.470 --> 00:04:31.890
power over model providers while facing

00:04:31.890 --> 00:04:34.290
more competition from smaller teams.

00:04:34.340 --> 00:04:36.900
Model labs may lose some scarcity and gain

00:04:36.900 --> 00:04:39.470
a much larger ecosystem built around their

00:04:39.780 --> 00:04:40.620
architecture.

00:04:40.660 --> 00:04:42.950
Now rotate once more to Germany and

00:04:43.060 --> 00:04:44.080
Singapore.

00:04:44.120 --> 00:04:46.310
Europe has committed 5 billion euros

00:04:46.360 --> 00:04:48.880
towards seven AI mega factories, trying to

00:04:48.960 --> 00:04:51.070
narrow the distance with the United States

00:04:51.070 --> 00:04:51.840
and China.

00:04:51.880 --> 00:04:54.560
Singapore is a deployment and finance hub.

00:04:54.600 --> 00:04:56.260
China is trying to balance the reach of

00:04:56.260 --> 00:04:57.870
open models with the control of

00:04:58.180 --> 00:05:00.200
strategically sensitive technology.

00:05:00.240 --> 00:05:02.300
The world is not choosing one winner.

00:05:02.340 --> 00:05:04.230
It is building several interlocking

00:05:04.230 --> 00:05:05.140
bottlenecks.

00:05:05.180 --> 00:05:07.290
That is why the signal to watch is not the

00:05:07.290 --> 00:05:08.820
loudest announcement.

00:05:08.860 --> 00:05:10.760
Watch the behavior underneath it.

00:05:10.800 --> 00:05:12.930
Are companies actually deploying open

00:05:12.930 --> 00:05:13.560
models?

00:05:13.600 --> 00:05:14.880
Are inference costs falling?

00:05:14.920 --> 00:05:16.400
Is usage expanding?

00:05:16.440 --> 00:05:18.500
Are AI revenues growing faster than

00:05:18.500 --> 00:05:19.710
capital spending?

00:05:19.760 --> 00:05:21.550
Are customers buying one provider's

00:05:21.550 --> 00:05:23.980
intelligence or building systems they can

00:05:23.980 --> 00:05:24.620
switch?

00:05:24.660 --> 00:05:26.910
The headline is not that open AI will

00:05:26.910 --> 00:05:28.200
crash the stock market.

00:05:28.480 --> 00:05:30.650
It is that open models are redrawing the

00:05:30.650 --> 00:05:31.560
profit map.

00:05:31.600 --> 00:05:33.890
The model may become the commodity layer.

00:05:34.040 --> 00:05:37.250
Compute, electricity, data, distribution,

00:05:37.250 --> 00:05:39.320
and trust may become the new toll booths.

00:05:39.360 --> 00:05:41.870
That is the market question for the next

00:05:41.870 --> 00:05:42.820
phase of AI.

00:05:42.860 --> 00:05:45.050
Not who has the cleverest model, but who

00:05:45.100 --> 00:05:47.720
still owns the bottleneck after everyone

00:05:47.840 --> 00:05:48.970
else can use one.
